  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Resilience and Livelihood Enhancement Project for Food-Insecure Households</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will assist 8352 vulnerable women and girls, returnees and internally displaced persons affected by crises in Akobo, Bor and Duk Counties of Jonglei State in South Sudan with Asset Creation and Livelihoods (ACL) interventions through provision of cash assistance.  Beneficiaries (1392 HHs) will  be engaged in Asset Creation and Livelihoods (ACL) activities which include construction or rehabilitation of community assets, provision of working tools, training and there after they receive  cash.  The project runs from 1 April 2025 to 31 August 2025.</narrative>
  </description>
